From the figure
$E A=60 \mathrm{~m}\left(T_1\right)$ and $D B=80 \mathrm{~m}\left(T_2\right)\angle D E C=\theta$ and $\angle B E C=2 \theta$
Now in $\triangle D E C$,

\tan \theta=\frac{D C}{A B}=\frac{20}{x}

and in $\triangle B E C$,

\tan 2 \theta=\frac{B C}{C E}=\frac{60}{x}

We know that

\tan 2 \theta=\frac{2 \tan \theta}{1-(\tan \theta)^2}

\begin{aligned}
&\Rightarrow \frac{60}{x}=\frac{2\left(\frac{20}{x}\right)}{1-\left(\frac{20}{x}\right)^2} \\
&\Rightarrow x^2=1200 \Rightarrow x=20 \sqrt{3}
\end{aligned}

